Well, I spent way too long on one game (i.e. had way too many real gems then I
could carry) and I finally left the dungeon with a score of 1512984.  I had
some 532 hit points, 320 energy points, -1 intrinsic armor class (when human)
and super strength beyond 18/99.  Oh, I started as a Ninja with a strength
of 9.

Have any of you bothered to play this long?  I've seen some people leaving
the dungeon with the amulate with scores in the 40000s.  So, did I get carried
away?  (At one point I had an armor class of -40.  How much overkill is this
anyway?)

One thing I've been curious about, though:  After I walked away with the
amulate I got occasional messages to the effect of "You feel a bit nervous"
and "You feel a bit disoriented."

The only thing I noticed is that I lost intrinsic teleportation capabilities
(^T).  Is this related to the messages?  Am I losing other abilities that I
didn't notice?

BTW:  I believe I played the full-blown NetHack 2.3 with all options enabled.

Sorry if this sounds like bragging, but I just wanted to see how greedy I
could be.

